{"title":"2024 BmMT Individual Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"border: 1px solid #444; background: #fff; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 20px auto; font-size: 90%; line-height: 1.6; font-family: sans-serif;\">\n<div style=\"background: #e0dbff; padding: 12px; text-align: center; border-bottom: 1px solid #444;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 110%; font-weight: bold; color: #4b3ba7;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_(Answer_Key)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual (Answer Key) (page does not exist)\">2024 BmMT Individual (Answer Key)</a></span><br />\n<span style=\"font-size: 95%; color: #6c5cb8;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Mini_Math_Tournament&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Berkeley Mini Math Tournament (page does not exist)\">BmMT Resources</a> • <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special:Upload&amp;wpDestFile=2024_BmMT_Individual.pdf\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual.pdf\">PDF</a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"padding: 15px 25px 15px 25px;\">\n<p style=\"font-weight: bold; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;\">Instructions</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 15px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">This test contains 20 short answer questions. All answers must be expressed in simplest form unless specified otherwise. Only answers written inside the boxes on the answer sheet will be considered for grading.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">Each correct answer is worth 1 point. Each incorrect or blank answer is worth 0 points.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">No calculators are permitted.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">Figures are not necessarily drawn to scale.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">You will have <b>60 minutes</b> working time to complete the test.</li>\n</ol>\n<div style=\"text-align: center; border-top: 1px solid #eee; padding-top: 12px; font-weight: bold; word-spacing: 2px;\">\n<p><a href=\"#Problem_1\">1</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_2\">2</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_3\">3</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_4\">4</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_5\">5</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_6\">6</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_7\">7</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_8\">8</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_9\">9</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_10\">10</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_11\">11</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_12\">12</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_13\">13</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_14\">14</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_15\">15</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_16\">16</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_17\">17</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_18\">18</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_19\">19</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_20\">20</a>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Nikhil has 20 BMT shirts and 24 BmMT shirts. Wen takes half of his shirts, and then Arjun takes half of his remaining shirts. How many shirts does Nikhil have left?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/90792f582bf19365ca5204e5f5a22ef91347d781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + \\frac{1}{2 + \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"79\" height=\"45\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rohit has a garden in the shape of a square with perimeter 2024. Youngmin has a lawn in the shape of a rectangle whose width is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b3872edca1b3b31074305b897398e8c1a558a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> the width of Rohit's garden and whose length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d9d23ee4b0ce23b0f61ac9fa8369b2aeed3c905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> the length of Rohit's garden. What is the area of Youngmin's lawn?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Anthony, Boris, and Carson are playing a game of frisbee! Anthony starts with the frisbee. On each turn, the player holding the frisbee throws it to someone else, after which the frisbee is either caught or dropped. If the frisbee is dropped, the nearest player picks it up. Throughout the game, Anthony throws the frisbee 8 times and catches it 6 times, Boris throws the frisbee 10 times and catches it 7 times, and Carson throws the frisbee 7 times and catches it 8 times. How many times is the frisbee dropped during the game?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the largest integer less than 2024 that leaves a remainder of 20 when divided by 24.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all prime numbers less than 50 that have only prime digits.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be two numbers taken from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/47860dd1b7554b04406b0eab8ce977070a98f94c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2^0, 2^1, 2^2, 2^3, \\dots, 2^{10}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"21\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6ca2af69871f83e1c3444d5209c0020879953c92.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy - (x + y) = 104.\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />\nWhat is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a859acebdd07c34704648be45c0daf108e2a29d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Thomas tosses a fair coin 3 times, and then Jefferson tosses the same coin 4 times. What is the probability that they flip exactly 3 heads in total?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00df1f45b96ff18990641ec2ae49bc43f23d9f59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> be the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive odd integers, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3cbf9ab1e976e485e5a8b8459491ffa0b561dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> be the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive even integers. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c44c2625dea4cd153371685654ff84c15d2e0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_1 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/418c45b07cc5ca1c9eea37d1c47b01a92d17db07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2 = 1 + 3 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" />. What is the value of the product\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377949332e15af0b81977c074dd4e945f3041041.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{O_1}{E_1} \\cdot \\frac{O_2}{E_2} \\cdot \\dots \\cdot \\frac{O_{2024}}{E_{2024}}?\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are chosen on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463d2f272d5bf52ebdd2a23f01b463cb78c2aa38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4378cdd55609a7569b7be61b7183a17f81254f46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDE = 125^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d1cdd9b9aa0fd977c1eed7834837b48c0831957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = 85^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7bbf36d9497baa24b11aada72461065b4bafb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEC + \\angle BAE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" /> in degrees?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all two-digit positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a factor of 2024 and the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c58d6d8a4599a0fd5a90aa2b46c54e234da296b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" /> is the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the product of all real numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, that satisfy\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a8b42ada777449e0104c5030e95f37c4d604b45.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^2 - 20x}{x^2 - 20x - 24} + \\frac{x^2 - 20x + 24}{x^2 - 20x} = 2?\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a hexagon with consecutive side lengths of 8, 6, 10, 8, 6, and 10, formed by attaching two right triangles with legs of length 6 and 8 to the top and bottom of a square, as shown in the diagram below. Compute the largest distance between two points in this hexagon.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Missing_Diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Missing Diagram (page does not exist)\">Template:Missing Diagram</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Kaity creates a list of all four-digit integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/9/f89e0ca688f912718b42d2324528b037f44fda43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{ABCD}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />, with distinct digits such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d78751a4aaa2a493b661a48a3c9af74c936f59c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3000 &lt; \\overline{ABCD} &lt; 6000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef84114c85c3e24e0f74d2a77edb4b21e4ec7b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible by 3, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd55ae0560e57945bc6dcc6d516728e01ba393f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BCD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible by 4, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4d6940466a7a03e13a4e42ac833d80ff3ba6d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DCB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible by 5, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96cbaad4a9c3440314b0d2951ca670cb73c1f04a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CBA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible by 6. Find the median of Kaity's list.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A permutation of a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers is any arrangement of its elements in a specific order. For example, permutations of the list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66ce7f76d142a721b5e74cb30696597cc0fde06b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> include <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aab0165cc9664c263e7d40598421090ee9358d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/7/e27589f15c8fce6e2ef60cce98d7f014b5e02e4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. Let a permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/0127c3b7bb51a8824cc01ac0092a50711a91e151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1, a_2, a_3, \\dots, a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" /> of the positive integers from 1 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, inclusive, be a <i>katamari</i> if, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd77e67d5e894bf1026f4cffd551f2856f52af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/700e8984054b35f81f801c7849c469d382f7bd02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i &lt; 2 + a_1 + a_2 + a_3 + \\dots + a_{i-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" /> holds. For example, the permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d4357988dd4f373952f63d610a4f81142944c089.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" /> is a katamari but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e0f172df17554a03fad22903945d8582b47de52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 4, 1, 2, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" /> is not. Compute the number of permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/4/12428358a89cacbe9ce6ffe57e2365c263d69951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2, 3, \\dots, 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" /> that are katamaris.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A positive integer is called square-free if it is not divisible by any perfect square greater than 1. Compute the sum of all positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, for which there exists a square-free positive integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/7371e478d919c41803f3932047acd489c69687f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> has 64 divisors.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let a sequence of integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f81465f6b02301397dd62f8fabd0eb65bc53077b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" />, be <i>anti-consecutive</i> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c2e88e1102144411d407e61de3971bb9928091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2024 \\le a_1 \\le 2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496d0c212c2edd49491eb46e9c2e2843a4cff47d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i + a_{i+1} = i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/290ca5ca749d5895f396eb7ef64a8c042b6997fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />. Over all anti-consecutive sequences of length 501, compute the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee99b604d774b01b423e9d6e6d1f67955347cfba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{501}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> that are divisible by 3.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be an equilateral triangle with side length 1. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/217779ccd30a73474c0f2cad20cac4ab2262a59e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_a, Ob,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9c83a604f853fd0cd8937d2b9b3a7ea714863d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> be three congruent circles inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f589508ca4f105cd721213b2ea57a2b1bbf6845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/471c719d8420d688129385e2704aea695cbbb208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9c83a604f853fd0cd8937d2b9b3a7ea714863d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and none of the circles intersect each other. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94ddc9fd5aa5e7173aa861b873c14e25e99f821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> be a circle inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> that is externally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d73a72b4293db26ff6aeecfb4477e1a17e80ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_a, O_b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9c83a604f853fd0cd8937d2b9b3a7ea714863d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />. What is the minimum possible sum of the areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f589508ca4f105cd721213b2ea57a2b1bbf6845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94ddc9fd5aa5e7173aa861b873c14e25e99f821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of the cubes of the divisors of 4200. Compute the last two digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jonathan has 46 indistinguishable blue balls, 3 indistinguishable red balls, and a green ball in a bin. He continuously draws balls from the bin without replacement until he draws the green ball. For instance, Jonathan might draw a red ball, followed by two blue balls, another red ball, and then the green ball, completing the process. Compute the number of possible sequences of draws that are possible under these conditions.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:BmMT_Individual_box&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:BmMT Individual box (page does not exist)\">Template:BmMT Individual box</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Mini_Math_Tournament&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Berkeley Mini Math Tournament (page does not exist)\">Berkeley Mini Math Tournament</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BmMT_Problems_and_Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"BmMT Problems and Solutions (page does not exist)\">BmMT Problems and Solutions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions\">Mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221046\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.072 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.127 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 513/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 62/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13974/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.010      1 -total\n 21.08%    2.321      1 Template:Missing_Diagram\n 20.84%    2.295      1 Template:BmMT_Individual_box\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37782:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017221046 and revision id 292069. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}